::ENG2_U04_L04_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Findings: A pre-order lunch pilot reduced unwanted trays. Student reminders helped more students complete forms. Which organization pattern fits best?{
=A. Cause and effect#Correct. The paragraph should explain how the form and reminders led to reduced waste.
~B. Chronological story plot#Incorrect. The goal is to explain research findings, not narrate a story.
~C. Random list#Incorrect. Research findings need logical organization.
~D. Definition only#Incorrect. The findings explain an effect, not only a definition.
}

::ENG2_U04_L04_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which sentence uses the best academic voice?{
~A. Lunch forms are super awesome and fixed everything.#Incorrect. This is informal and exaggerated.
=B. Pre-order lunch forms may reduce waste when staff prepare meals from student selections.#Correct. This is clear, measured, and source-based.
~C. Everybody should just do lunch forms because I said so.#Incorrect. This is informal and unsupported.
~D. Forms are, like, the best thing ever.#Incorrect. This is informal and biased.
}

::ENG2_U04_L04_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.R.05] Findings: Gardens provide observations. Journals help students record observations. Teacher routines connect observations to vocabulary. Which structure best explains these findings?{
~A. Unrelated details#Incorrect. The findings are connected.
~B. Compare and contrast two opposite sides#Incorrect. The findings do not mainly show opposing sides.
=C. Sequence or process because each step builds science learning.#Correct. The findings show a process from observation to recording to vocabulary use.
~D. Definition only#Incorrect. The findings explain a process, not just a term.
}

::ENG2_U04_L04_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which transition best shows cause and effect?{
~A. For example#Incorrect. This introduces an example, not necessarily an effect.
~B. On the other hand#Incorrect. This signals contrast.
~C. In addition#Incorrect. This adds information but does not directly show effect.
=D. As a result#Correct. This transition signals an effect.
}

::ENG2_U04_L04_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which topic sentence best fits an expository paragraph about school gardens and science learning?{
~A. School gardens are cool and everyone knows it.#Incorrect. This is informal and unsupported.
=B. A school garden can support science learning by giving students observations to record, compare, and explain.#Correct. This sentence previews the explanation with academic voice.
~C. Gardens have dirt.#Incorrect. This is too narrow and does not preview the paragraph.
~D. I like science sometimes.#Incorrect. This is personal and not expository.
}
